YEAH!  I finally won!  it took some luck and a massive amount of
patience and just plain stubbornness, but I finally managed to beat
Nethack... go me.

I've only ever played wizards; they're the coolest to me, since they
can cast all those sweet high-level spells eventually.  Anyway, this
one started out with a spellbook of Charm Monster, and found create
monster before getting to mine town.  Magic Lamp - wished for a ring of
slow digestion, locked myself inside the (coaligned) temple and spent ~
40K turns sacrificing.  That was where the stubbornness part came in :)

By the time I left, the rest of the game was a letdown.  I'd gotten all
the intrinsics that you can possibly get from praying, including naked
AC 0, plus loads of other good stuff, including a wand of wishing 0:3.
I used it on armor (SDSM, speed boots, gauntlets of dexterity, helm of
brilliance), Frost Brand, a magic marker (gotta get some genocide
scrolls somehow; L's and h's are bad for my health), and an amulet of
Life Saving (I'm always making some dumb mistake or other).  I'd also
found and proofed a +3 small shield and an oilskin cloak, although I
was still wearing magic resistance for now, as well as a bag of
holding.  Not bad at all.

I basically pounded everything else flat after that; it was interesting
but I was never really afraid I might die.  I camped out again at the
quest goal level, and didn't leave until I was level 30 (wraiths appear
relatively often when creating monsters on that level) and had a silver
dragon called Chrome as a pet.  I found a saddle soon after, and rode
Chrome for quite a while.  I went next to the castle, cleaned it out,
and got several more dragons as pets.  By the time I'd used up the
castle wand I had an armor class of -53, which I was to keep for the
rest of the game.  I was wearing a t-shirt, SDSM, oilskin cloak, helm
of brilliance, gauntlets of dexterity, speed boots, small shield... you
get the picture.

Hell was uneventful, except that I ran across a couple of major demons
that I've never even heard of before, even though I've made it to the
Astral Plane before.  Their names were Dispater and Geryon, and Orcus
summoned them as I was whomping on him.  Anyway, besides this I just
sprinted through and grabbed the artifacts I needed.  By this point
Chrome had gone down (I didn't notice it at the time, just figured out
suddenly that I wasn't riding a dragon and retraced my steps until I
found my saddle and Chrome's scales).  So anyway, I was riding Sparky
II (the second blue dragon I'd tamed; his brother Sparky had been
killed by Orcus' wand of death) and suddenly he's gone too, don't know
how.  Ah well.  I had about eleven million dragons by then, so I was
riding for the rest of the game.

Killed the wizard easily, did the bell-candles-book thing, grabbed the
Amulet and quaffed a cursed potion of gain level to save time.  Made it
to the top real quick (compared to my other time doing it at least) and
left the dungeon with 4 dragons.  However, I'd forgotten Charm Monster
by then and my spellbook was too faint to be reread, and I was out of
magic markers.  Oh well.

To start up on the Plane of Earth I gave Rodney the finger, but it
bounced back and killed my dragon.  Saddled up Rainman (yellow) and
went for the exit like crazy.  I made it easily, but Flame V (red
dragon) was still eating or something so all I had left for dragons was
Rainman and Misty (grey).  On the plane of Air I was doing well until 2
ki-rins started summoning massive hordes of monsters, including an air
elemental that threw me off of Rainman.  I took off my rings of slow
digestion and protection, and wore conflict and levitation (I'd kept
levitation handy all along; I KNEW something like that was going to
happen).  I killed everything, but Rainman got killed and Misty was my
last dragon.  However, I couldn't find Rainman's saddle so I just gave
up and left without a mount.  On the plane of Fire I had an easy time,
except that Misty got surrounded and killed by some salamanders and the
like.  On the Plane of Water, I suddenly realized that I was out of
scrolls of gold detection.  I have no idea what happened to that last
one.  I searched for a while, and was just starting to think I might
starve to death right there when I realized that I could just take out
all of my spare scrolls and cast polymorph at them until I got another
gold detection.  I did this, and it worked, although the gold detection
one was one of the last 5 or so left out of like 20.  I left the plane
of water, wearing rings of protection and slow digestion.  I tried the
right altar first, but it was to Ptah.  Tried middle next, and it was
to Thoth.  Finally made it to the left altar and, of course, it was to
Anhur, my god.  Pounded a last few losers out of my way, and sacrificed
the Amulet.  Yay!

That AC was awesome... even on the Astral Plane my HP always stayed
within like 15 or 20 of maximum.

